<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      SCHAT requests two permissions, both of which exist to do one visible thing.

      INTERNET  — reach the relay the user configured. The server routes ciphertext and
                  stores public prekeys; it never sees a message.

      CAMERA    — read a QR code, so that two devices can exchange a 64-character identity
                  key without anybody typing it. Typing it by hand is not merely tedious:
                  one wrong character produces the same "no bundle published for that
                  identity" error as a peer that never published, so the mistake is
                  indistinguishable from the symptom.

      The camera is opened ONLY while the scan screen is on screen, and the frames are
      decoded in memory and dropped. Nothing is photographed, stored, or transmitted —
      QrScannerScreen is the only code in the app that touches the camera, and it hands
      back a decoded string.

      Still deliberately absent, and it must stay that way: READ_CONTACTS, any location
      permission, READ_PHONE_STATE, READ_SMS, RECORD_AUDIO, and every advertising
      identifier. SCHAT.md section 12.5 promises the app cannot collect what it never asks
      for, and the manifest is where that promise is enforced.

      Adding CAMERA weakens the older claim that SCHAT requests nothing but network
      access. Three places carried that claim — SCHAT.md (sections 12.6 and 14.4),
      docs/FAQ.md and docs/DEVICE-TEST.md — and all three were corrected in the same
      change rather than left to go stale.
    -->
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.INTERNET" />
    <uses-permission android:name="android.permission.CAMERA" />

    <!--
      required="false" so that a device without a camera can still install SCHAT. Scanning
      is a convenience; the identity can always be pasted by hand, and refusing the whole
      application over a missing camera would be absurd.
    -->
    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.hardware.camera"
        android:required="false" />
    <uses-feature
        android:name="android.hardware.camera.autofocus"
        android:required="false" />

    <application
        android:name=".SchatApplication"
        android:allowBackup="false"
        android:dataExtractionRules="@xml/data_extraction_rules"
        android:fullBackupContent="false"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:roundIcon="@mipmap/ic_launcher_round"
        android:label="@string/app_name"
        android:supportsRtl="true"
        android:theme="@style/Theme.Schat">

        <activity
            android:name=".MainActivity"
            android:exported="true"
            android:label="@string/app_name"
            android:theme="@style/Theme.Schat"
            android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize">
            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
    </application>

</manifest>
